      "title": "Income Tax Rates",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "For incomes of profit-seeking business enterprises the following rates shall be imposed:",
          "columns": [
            "Item",
            "Rate"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(a)",
              "2 per cent on profits less than 5 per cent of actual capital"
            ],
            [
              "(b)",
              "4 per cent on profits between 10 and 15 per cent of actual capital"
            ],
            [
              "(c)",
              "6 per cent on profits between 15 and 20 per cent of actual capital"
            ],
            [
              "(d)",
              "8 per cent on profits between 20 and 25 per cent of actual capital"
            ],
            [
              "(e)",
              "10 per cent on profits above 25 per cent of actual capital"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "For earnings of business establishments, which cannot be calculated on the basis of the preceding categories, the following rates shall be imposed:",
          "columns": [
            "Item",
            "Rate"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(a)",
              "Incomes not exceeding $100 free"
            ],
            [
              "(b)",
              "3 per cent on earnings $100 to $1,000"
            ],
            [
              "(c)",
              "4 per cent on earning $1,000 to $2,500"
            ],
            [
              "(d)",
              "6 per cent on earnings $2,500 to $5,000"
            ],
            [
              "(e)",
              "1 per cent for every $1,000 above $5,000"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Income tax rates on emoluments and salaries shall be as follows: On average monthly incomes",
          "columns": [
            "Item",
            "Rate"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(a)",
              "$30 to $60, 5 cents on every $10"
            ],
            [
              "(b)",
              "$60 to $100, 10 cents on every $10 above $60"
            ],
            [
              "(c)",
              "$100 to $200, 20 cents on every $10 above $100"
            ],
            [
              "(d)",
              "$200 to $300, 30 cents on every $10 above $200"
            ],
            [
              "(e)",
              "$300 to $400, 40 cents on every $10 above $300"
            ],
            [
              "(f)",
              "$400 to $500, 60 cents on every $10 above $400"
            ],
            [
              "(g)",
              "$500 to $600, 80 cents on every $10 above $500"
            ],
            [
              "(h)",
              "$600 to $700, $1 on every $10 above $600"
            ],
            [
              "(i)",
              "$700 to $800, $1.20 on every $10 above $700"
            ],
            [
              "(j)",
              "Above $800, 20 cents on every $10 of first $100 above $800 until it reaches $2 on every $10"
            ],
            [
              "(k)",
              "No tax on amounts above any mark but below $5 in difference, while amounts above $5 shall be counted as $10"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Rate schedules printed as lettered lists; transcribed verbatim, one row per item.",
        "Part 1 as printed jumps from 'less than 5 per cent' (a) to 'between 10 and 15' (b): the 5-10 per cent bracket is not printed.",
        "Following the lists the text reads: 'Flat rate of 5 per cent shall be imposed on interest accrued from Government bonds, on corporation debentures and banking deposits.' (not a table row)."
      ],
      "id": "p2-0014_4",
