      "table_no": null,
      "title": "[Groups of dutiable documents under the New Provisional Regulations for stamp duties, 1927]",
      "caption_extra": "New Provisional Regulations for stamp duties were promulgated by the National Government in July, 1927, which divided dutiable documents into four groups. Group I comprises fifteen kinds of documents grouped under three classes:—",
      "continued": false,
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": null,
          "columns": [
            "Group",
            "Class",
            "Documents",
            "Stamp duty"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Group I",
              "Class A (seven kinds)",
              "bills, receipts for goods deposited, receipts for goods hired, pawn-tickets, value of $4 upwards, etc.",
              "one cent stamp"
            ],
            [
              "Group I",
              "Class B (six kinds)",
              "invoices, agreements for hire, receipts for advance orders, etc.",
              "1 cent stamp if value between $1 and $10, otherwise 2 cent stamp"
            ],
            [
              "Group I",
              "Class C (two kinds)",
              "bank pass-books and account books of business houses",
              "each book, 10 cent stamp"
            ],
            [
              "Group II (fourteen kinds)",
              "",
              "Bills of lading, insurance policies, deposit receipts, share certificates, checks, drafts, loan agreements, etc.",
              "1 cent stamp if value between $1 and $10, 2 cent if over $10 and under $100, 4 cent over $100 and under $500, 10 cent over $500 and under $1,000, 20 cent over $1,000 and under $5,000, 50 cent over $5,000 and under $10,000, $1 over $10,000 and under $50,000, $1.50 if $50,000 or upwards"
            ],
            [
              "Group III (45 kinds)",
              "",
              "Passports, certificates, testimonials, permits, licences, charters, etc.",
              "stamp duty varies from 1 cent to $10"
            ],
            [
              "Group IV (four kinds)",
              "",
              "to be affixed on foreign wines and aerated water bottles, alcohol, fireworks, etc.",
              "ranging from 2 cents for aerated water, to $10 for alcohol"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        "With the exception of those to be affixed on the articles included in Group IV, the stamps will partake of the following five colors: buff (1 cent), green (2 cent), red (10 cent), purple (50 cent), blue ($1)."
      ],
      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Set out in the source as an indented list of groups/classes; converted to a table, wording verbatim, parenthesised stamp rates moved to the Stamp duty column.",
        "Group I (Classes A-C) on p. 223 (p2-0014); Groups II-IV on p. 224 (p2-0015, batch C10's range) — finished here per the continuation rule.",
        "The Tax Exemptions list on p. 224 and the Tariff Rates of Chinese Maritime Customs table on p. 225 are left to batch C10."
      ],
      "id": "p2-0014_7",
      "scans": [
        {
          "label": "scan part 2, leaf 14",
